business;","section":"If we fail to manage our growth effectively, our business, financial condition and results of operations may be harmed.","block":408,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001585521-26-000030","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2026-01-31","cik":"0001585521","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1585521/000158552126000030/zm-20260131.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c384a10fcc4ec0f66889bfdc524bf32a8142a8b297d00a260b3aafb243163ce6.bin","sha256":"c384a10fcc4ec0f66889bfdc524bf32a8142a8b297d00a260b3aafb243163ce6"}},{"id":"6098179ebc278eded704dca162e50474da2a66efcc7266e7b33fa9c60c2726e7","quote":"•generally longer payment cycles and greater difficulty in collecting accounts receivable, a risk that may increase as a result of recent macroeconomic conditions, such as high inflation, recessionary environments, recent bank failures and related uncertainties, and fluctuations in foreign currency exchange rates, weighing on our customers' ability to pay for our service on a timely basis;","context":"•changes in diplomatic and trade relationships, including the continuing deterioration in diplomatic relations between the United States and China, or deterioration in diplomatic relations between the United States and countries with which the United States has traditionally enjoyed close ties and alliances, and ongoing military conflicts;","section":"If we fail to manage our growth effectively, our business, financial condition and results of operations may be harmed.","block":409,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001585521-26-000030","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2026-01-31","cik":"0001585521","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1585521/000158552126000030/zm-20260131.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c384a10fcc4ec0f66889bfdc524bf32a8142a8b297d00a2